    <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="_yNtmkFRmEem5ec_9KiA7Yg" name="Diagrams"/>
    <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="_yNuNoFRmEem5ec_9KiA7Yg" name="Imports">
      <packageImport xmi:type="uml:PackageImport" xmi:id="_6sAokFRmEem5ec_9KiA7Yg">
        <importedPackage xmi:type="uml:Model" href="CommonDataTypes/ImplementationCommonDataTypes.uml#_-lRh4FDNEeWpFusmeDrF3w"/>
      </packageImport>
      <packageImport xmi:type="uml:PackageImport" xmi:id="_EHGUUKSHEemZx_PrWGDYjw">
        <importedPackage xmi:type="uml:Package" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_oGqilVLNEeO75dO39GbF8Q"/>
      </packageImport>
    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="_yNuNoVRmEem5ec_9KiA7Yg" name="Interfaces">
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="_jmLNkKecEe2VB6m2xY-hwQ" name="Layer1AggregationProfileOperations">
        <ownedOperation xmi:type="uml:Operation" xmi:id="_JAPNgeOmEe-GceXpRDU6RA" name="createLayer1AggregationProfile">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_JAPNguOmEe-GceXpRDU6RA" annotatedElement="_JAPNgeOmEe-GceXpRDU6RA">
            <body>Creates a Layer1Aggregation with the group of UUIDs of LTPs of layer protocol name HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure and returns the UUID of the resulting Layer1Aggregation Profile. Existing configurations made obsolete by this configuration change are purged in the background. The following error-messages are to be send, if the operation would fail: #[onf:Referenced object is invalid.]#, if any of the referenced objects does not exist or is of the wrong type. #[onf:Referenced object is not capable.]#, if the interface represented by any of the referenced HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure is not supporting being added to the aggregation group. #[onf:Wished change contradicts existing configuration.]#, if the interface represented by any of the referenced HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure is already in use in another aggregation group. #[onf:Wished changes are not consistent. ]#, if e.g. the group of referenced HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure is not complete for creating the aggregation group. #[onf:Resources not available.]#, if the maximum number of aggregation groups has already been configured. #[onf:Configuration value out of range of hardware capabilities.]#, if the device is not supporting switching aggregation groups on/off during instantiation.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_JAPNg-OmEe-GceXpRDU6RA" name="_servingStructureList" isUnique="false" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_JAPNhOOmEe-GceXpRDU6RA" annotatedElement="_JAPNg-OmEe-GceXpRDU6RA">
              <body>List of UUIDs of LogicalTerminationPoints with LayerProtocol::layerProtocolName==LAYER_PROTOCOL_NAME_TYPE_HYBRID_MW_STRUCTURE_LAYER or LAYER_PROTOCOL_NAME_TYPE_PURE_ETHERNET_STRUCTURE_LAYER.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_eEpDMFX4EeOVGaP4lO41SQ"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="_JAPNheOmEe-GceXpRDU6RA"/>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="_JAPNhuOmEe-GceXpRDU6RA" value="*"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_ZRRzICTNEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" name="aggregationGroupIsOn" isUnique="false">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_ZRRzISTNEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" annotatedElement="_ZRRzICTNEfCBVvqBo6ti9w">
              <body>If true, the layer 1 aggregation group will be configured to be activated, so it is forwarding traffic to the serving layers.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#Boolean"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_L5FVIPNYEe-Vg_DIy13D6A" name="_resultingLayer1AggregationProfile" isUnique="false" direction="out">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_L5FVIfNYEe-Vg_DIy13D6A" annotatedElement="_L5FVIPNYEe-Vg_DIy13D6A">
              <body>UUID of the resulting Profile with profileName==PROFILE_NAME_TYPE_LAYER_1_AGGREGATION_PROFILE that has just been created.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_GLc2MJ47Eemkbek818V8NQ"/>
          </ownedParameter>
        </ownedOperation>
        <ownedOperation xmi:type="uml:Operation" xmi:id="_AnyfcCTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" name="updateLayer1AggregationProfile">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_AnyfcSTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" annotatedElement="_AnyfcCTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w">
            <body>Updates the configuration of the referenced layer1AggregationProfile with the group of UUIDs of LTPs of layer protocol name HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure and the status of the on/off switch and returns the UUID of the resulting Layer1Aggregation Profile. Existing configurations made obsolete by this configuration change are purged in the background. The following error-messages are to be send, if the operation would fail: #[onf:Referenced object is invalid.]#, if any of the referenced objects does not exist or is of the wrong type. #[onf:Referenced object is not capable.]#, if the interface represented by any of the referenced HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure is not supporting being added to the aggregation group. #[onf:Wished change contradicts existing configuration.]#, if the interface represented by any of the referenced HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure is already in use in another aggregation group. #[onf:Wished changes are not consistent. ]#, if e.g. the group of referenced HybridMwStructure or PureEthernetStructure is not complete for creating the aggregation group. #[onf:Configuration value out of range of hardware capabilities.]#, if the device is not supporting switching aggregation groups on/off.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_AnyfciTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" name="_layer1AggregationProfile" isUnique="false" effect="update">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_AnyfcyTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" annotatedElement="_AnyfciTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w">
              <body>UUID of an existing Profile with profileName==PROFILE_NAME_TYPE_LAYER_1_AGGREGATION_PROFILE that shall be re-configured.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_GLc2MJ47Eemkbek818V8NQ"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="_AnyfdCTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" value="1"/>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="_AnyfdSTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" value="1"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_AnyfdiTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" name="_servingStructureList" isUnique="false" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_AnyfdyTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" annotatedElement="_AnyfdiTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w">
              <body>List of UUIDs of LogicalTerminationPoints with LayerProtocol::layerProtocolName==LAYER_PROTOCOL_NAME_TYPE_HYBRID_MW_STRUCTURE_LAYER or LAYER_PROTOCOL_NAME_TYPE_PURE_ETHERNET_STRUCTURE_LAYER.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_eEpDMFX4EeOVGaP4lO41SQ"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="_AnyfeCTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" value="1"/>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="_AnyfeSTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" value="*"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_AnyfeiTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" name="aggregationGroupIsOn" isUnique="false">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_AnyfeyTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" annotatedElement="_AnyfeiTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w">
              <body>If true, the layer 1 aggregation group will be configured to be activated, so it is forwarding traffic to the serving layers.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#Boolean"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_AnyffCTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" name="_resultingLayer1AggregationProfile" isUnique="false" direction="out">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_AnyffSTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w" annotatedElement="_AnyffCTOEfCBVvqBo6ti9w">
              <body>UUID of the Profile with profileName==PROFILE_NAME_TYPE_LAYER_1_AGGREGATION_PROFILE that resulted from the update.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_GLc2MJ47Eemkbek818V8NQ"/>
          </ownedParameter>
        </ownedOperation>
        <ownedOperation xmi:type="uml:Operation" xmi:id="_79dvQKehEe2VB6m2xY-hwQ" name="deleteLayer1AggregationProfile">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_sXe5IPNjEe-Vg_DIy13D6A" annotatedElement="_79dvQKehEe2VB6m2xY-hwQ">
            <body>Deletes the Layer1Aggregation that is identified in the input and creates all logical objects that are required for representing the initial state of the device again. The following error-message is to be send, if the operation would fail: #[onf:Layer1AggregationProfile cannot be deleted.]#, if the referenced object cannot be deleted.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_79dvQaehEe2VB6m2xY-hwQ" name="_obsoleteLayer1AggregationProfile" isUnique="false" effect="delete">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_79dvQqehEe2VB6m2xY-hwQ" annotatedElement="_79dvQaehEe2VB6m2xY-hwQ">
              <body>UUID of the instance of Layer1AggregationProfile (ProfileNameType==PROFILE_NAME_TYPE_LAYER_1_AGGREGATION_PROFILE) that shall be deleted.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_GLc2MJ47Eemkbek818V8NQ"/>
          </ownedParameter>
        </ownedOperation>
        <ownedOperation xmi:type="uml:Operation" xmi:id="_N1tkcAlSEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="provideCapabilitiesOfLayer1Aggregation">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_N1tkcQlSEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_N1tkcAlSEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
            <body>Defines the general capabilities of the layer 1 aggregation implementation on the device.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_N1tkcglSEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="minimumNumberOfServers" isUnique="false" direction="out" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_xvVuoAlcEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_N1tkcglSEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
              <body>Defines the minimum number of LTPs that need to be referenced in the _servingStructureList input parameter of the createLayer1AggregationProfile operation.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#Integer"/>
            <defaultValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="_7gX_wEOEEfCedKIEsoQ9cg"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_paDpQAldEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="deactivatingAnAggrationGroupIsAvail" isUnique="false" direction="out" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_KhiAcAleEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_paDpQAldEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
              <body>If true, the device supports temporary disable/enable of a layer 1 aggregation group.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#Boolean"/>
            <defaultValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralBoolean" xmi:id="_paDpQQldEfCRnOaLgaHsgg"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_KTt8AAlgEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="maximumNumberOfAggregationGroups" isUnique="false" direction="out" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_KTt8AQlgEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_KTt8AAlgEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
              <body>Maximum number of layer 1 aggregation groups that can be configured on the device.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#Integer"/>
            <defaultValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="_uJ3RoEOEEfCedKIEsoQ9cg"/>
          </ownedParameter>
        </ownedOperation>
        <ownedOperation xmi:type="uml:Operation" xmi:id="_QkFu4AlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="provideCapabilitiesOfLayer1AggregationGroup">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_QkFu4QlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_QkFu4AlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
            <body>Defines the capabilities that are specific to the referenced layer 1 aggregation group. The following error-message is to be send, if the operation would fail: #[onf:Referenced object is invalid.]#, if the referenced objects does not exist or is of the wrong type.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_bdEDkAlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="_layer1AggregationProfile" isUnique="false" effect="delete">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_bdEDkQlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_bdEDkAlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
              <body>UUID of the instance of Layer1AggregationProfile (ProfileNameType==PROFILE_NAME_TYPE_LAYER_1_AGGREGATION_PROFILE) for which the capability information shall be provided.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="../ONF%20CoreMode%20pruned%20and%20refactored%20as%20device%20model/CoreModel.pnr.uml#_GLc2MJ47Eemkbek818V8NQ"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_QkFu5AlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="maximumNumberOfServers" isUnique="false" direction="out" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_25z9gAleEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_QkFu5AlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
              <body>Defines the maximum number of LTPs that might be referenced in the _servingStructureList input parameter of the updateLayer1AggregationProfile operation, while updating a referenced layer 1 aggregation group.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#Integer"/>
            <defaultValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="_QkFu5QlVEfCRnOaLgaHsgg"/>
          </ownedParameter>
          <ownedParameter xmi:type="uml:Parameter" xmi:id="_JtI5oAlfEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" name="_listOfStructureLtpsThatMightBeAdded" isUnique="false" direction="out" effect="read">
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_JtI5oQlfEfCRnOaLgaHsgg" annotatedElement="_JtI5oAlfEfCRnOaLgaHsgg">
